      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_City%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between 1836 and 1861, families from Tennessee, North Carolina, and Virginia moved into the area that would become Cave City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cavecity.us/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "When Sharp County formed in 1868, the area now known as Cave City was still part of Independence County, before the 1875 boundary shift.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cavecity.us/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cave City hosts an annual July festival celebrating its award‑winning “world’s sweetest” watermelons.",
